⚙️ The God Machines of the Eternal Trinity 永恒三位一体的神机

Across the fractured ruins of the Sovereigns of Aeons, three civilizations unearthed the forbidden texts of the Necronomium and shards of the Silver Key.
With hubris to rival their forerunners, each civilization forged a God Machine — a colossal war-engine that was less machine and more living paradox.
Their hearts are powered by the Silver Key Shards, their bodies inscribed with equations and invocations torn from the Necronomium.
Each God Machine is worshiped as a divine avatar, feared even by the ones who built them.

🌅 Solar Colossus 太阳巨像 (Sunborn God Machine)
Forged upon the desert forges of Erythra, the Solar Colossus was carved from the buried citadels of glass and bound with the Ember of Dawn. Its core houses the Sunborn’s shard of the Silver Key, which fuels an eternal furnace.
Its mere presence scorches the battlefield; armies ignite like offerings, and night turns to endless noon.
The Necronomium fragment woven into its design describes “The Flame that Burns Beyond Dawn”, and so the Solar Colossus is revered as the Sunborn’s proof of divine succession.

🌑 Dreadnut 巨惧蛞 (Voidhollow God Machine)
Forged in the tombs of N’kai, the Dreadnut was built not as a beacon, but as a vessel of annihilation. Its body is a hollow fortress, inscribed with the Necronomium’s prophecy of “The Fang that Devours Memory.”
Its Silver Key shard does not shine — it consumes. It drinks warmth, sound, and even history from the world around it. To behold the Dreadnut is to risk being forgotten, erased from records and memory alike.
